    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>Another way is to use the <code>-t</code> open for <code>ssh</code>:</p>
<pre><code>ssh -t user@server "sudo script"
</code></pre>
<p>See <a href=3D"https://linuxcommand.org/lc3_man_pages/ssh1.html" rel=3D"=
noreferrer"><code>man ssh</code></a>:</p>
<pre><code> -t      Force pseudo-tty allocation.  This can be used to execu=
te arbi-
         trary screen-based programs on a remote machine, which can be
         very useful, e.g., when implementing menu services.  Multiple -t
         options force tty allocation, even if ssh has no local tty.
</code></pre>
    </div>
